# Conformance probe pack for gate blocks (spec 0.17, Decode): one key at two
# locators, the first inside a block. Fixed `bits` layout, least significant
# bit first. Public. No kinds. One byte per word. Exercises: a line in a block
# that does not hold counts as a line whose locator is absent, so decode takes
# the key's next line; encode opens the block for the key and writes both.
#
#   byte 0       bit 0: byte 1 holds x
#   byte 1       x, when bit 0 is 1
#   byte 2       x
format     conformance-gates-lines
version    0.17.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
if      0:0:1  1
  field probe.x   0:8:8    uint
end
field   probe.x   0:16:8   uint
